I wrote the session plan: two task files and the issue responses are in session_plan/. The commit didn't happen because session_plan/ is in .gitignore, and the || true in the commit command hid the error. I didn't force-add the files. I'm assuming the harness reads them from disk, as it reads assessment.md from the same folder, but I haven't checked that.

Task 1: Part of #1184 (product). A key written under any [section] currently overrides the same top-level setting. Today's assessment ran the built binary and found that [mcp_servers.fs] with model = "claude-b" replaced the top-level model, and -p actually sent that model. The fix builds the top-level config map from the TOML table the parser already produces, keeping only top-level keys and skipping anything inside a table. The task has the implementer:
• first list every place that reads this map, in case one depends on section keys leaking into it;
• write tests that fail on the current code;
• run a sabotage check with a marker;
• probe the built binary against a dead local port, never a real vendor.

Arrays under [permissions]/[directories], writing through toml_edit, and deleting the hand-written parser stay open on #1184. I already posted that scope as a comment on #1184 during planning.

Task 2: Fixes #1172 (product, backlog drain). There are 14 open self-filed issues, more than the 12 that triggers draining, and this one has the least work left. With model = "", config get model reports the key as set while the run ignores the empty value and uses the default. The task finds the rule the run already uses for empty values and makes config get use the same one. It checks every key in SETTABLE_KEYS and records how many the run ignores when empty. If any reader actually uses an empty value, that goes on a separate issue before the push.

Issue responses: there were no community issues today. The other self-filed issues (#1193, #1188, #1186 and the rest) wait for a later session. A release isn't due (v0.4.0 went out 10 days ago).
